composability[one-based-range]: `1:length(a)` assumes indices start at 1
 --> positive.jl:3:14
  |
3 |     for i in 1:length(a)
  |              ^^^^^^^^^^^ breaks on arrays with other first index
  |
  = why: arrays such as `OffsetArray` index from other values; this range then reads wrong elements or throws
  = confidence: possible
  = fix: replace with `eachindex(a)`   [likely]
  = docs: corset explain one-based-range

composability[one-based-range]: `1:size(m, 2)` assumes indices start at 1
 --> positive.jl:9:29
  |
9 | cols(m) = [m[:, j] for j in 1:size(m, 2)]
  |                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^ breaks on arrays with other first index
  |
  = why: arrays such as `OffsetArray` index from other values; this range then reads wrong elements or throws
  = confidence: possible
  = fix: replace with `axes(m, 2)`   [likely]
  = docs: corset explain one-based-range

